  "findings": [],
  "closedReviewFindings": [
    {
      "id": "sensitive-parser-diagnostics-bypass",
      "severity": "P1",
      "originalEvidence": "The initial task-level platform.log suppression did not cover AnalyzeByJSonPath class Logger FINE records with Throwable or NetworkUtils absoluteURL printOnDebug(Throwable). Submitted text incorporated into a failing path/URL could reach formatted diagnostics. Initial tests observed only a different logger record.message.",
      "v2Correction": "AnalyzeRule and AnalyzeUrl pass the same existing task platform diagnostic callback to the existing JSONPath and URL helpers. RulePlatform retains the original logger/FINE/Throwable behavior for ordinary execution; ProductionRulePlatform suppresses it for sensitive login tasks. No global logger filter, ThreadLocal, new parser or new state owner was added. NetworkUtils keeps the original two-argument Java overloads.",
      "validation": "The existing fourth-method suite passes after the privacy method captures both logger classes with SimpleFormatter including Throwable, first proves ordinary diagnostics observable, then checks sensitive scalar/list/element JSONPath and malformed URL canaries plus authored direct/form log/error cases."
    },
    {
      "id": "traditional-caller-retained-map-and-empty-value-contract",
      "severity": "P2",
      "originalEvidence": "Locked SourceLoginDialog817-829 starts from viewModel.loginInfo and overlays visible text/password edits; line824 preserves explicit empty String. Lines832-840 do not impose an all-text-required gate. Initial new caller reduced visible fields from an empty map and used the legacy required/default-restoring helpers, dropping hidden tokens and rejecting/replacing valid empty optional values.",
      "v2Correction": "Only traditional confirmation uses a complete existing values snapshot and a pure off-main helper that overwrites text/password with values[name] ?? default ?? empty. Hidden keys and explicit empty edits survive; native submission skips the legacy required gate. Nontraditional validation/currentFormValues/resolvedValue and unrelated menu/dynamic routes retain their prior behavior.",
      "validation": "The existing blankLoginFieldIsRequired method gains helper assertions for edited/hidden/empty/optional/default and actually-empty maps without a new test definition. Those Swift assertions remain unexecuted until SDK acceptance."
    }
  ],
  "reviewedProperties": [
    "The actual existing form confirmation consumer calls BookSourceFetcher.shared.mainJSService.originalFormLogin only for traditional text sources. It reuses the current source actor lock, actual source revision, NativeLegadoOriginalPreviewExecutor, LegadoRuntimeProcess and sole JVM/Rhino environment; there is no original-source JSC fallback.",
    "BaseSource.login retains getLoginJs trim/unwrap plus mandatory login.apply(this) or throw, and ignores completion values. The finite form operation stores accepted nonempty credentials before optional JS, stops on known false put, and removes raw credentials without executing JS for an empty map within its supported non-browser/non-v2 domain.",
    "The standalone dialog supplies actual null Book/Chapter, a real Java form Map result and isLongClick=false. OriginalSourceLoginHost borrows that source/task/environment and lazy existing AnalyzeRule. Its close releases only borrowed parser resources and cannot close the owning environment.",
    "Arbitrary returned JS JSON never becomes loginHeader. Only explicit source.putLoginHeader and existing original HTTP/Cookie owner operations can change those stores. Submitted raw secrets use the prior dedicated source.login-info/LoginManager Keychain route; no generic secret cache, alternate HTTP stack or new owner is introduced.",
    "Browser/UI-v2 routes are explicitly rejected before this finite native operation mutates credentials; host browser/UI/clipboard/toast methods remain typed unsupported. These are documented capability boundaries, not full SourceLoginJsExtensions support.",
    "The Package entry uses existing executeOriginal task/deadline/cancellation/effect mechanisms. Source-lock wait shares the finite thirty-second iOS deadline, which is disclosed separately from Android lifecycle cancellation. Accepted credential receipts survive later JS/HTTP error or cancellation, while the actual held-HTTP regression permits no late explicit header.",
    "Native executor closes the real session and revokes the same source grant through both success and failure; the service merges issued effect facts into sanitized errors. The owned UI task cancels on disappearance and suppresses late alerts.",
    "Form Runtime errors and direct source.login errors use static code-only messages; authored logs and the covered parser/URL Throwable diagnostics respect the same task-sensitive flag. Swift service/UI expose only static code and effect count, without arbitrary Error descriptions or request/body/credential text.",
    "The new Native fixture uses the existing real Swift BookSource JSON path, retaining its typed ruleContent admission, and calls the actual product service/owners. It remains only a definition until actual native execution.",
    "UI native components, presentation/title/style and prior previews are preserved. The two reused outcome/error localization keys were independently found in all five language tables."
  ],
